From 5fe7cc99e3311048b5827e0b32fc6833f59a4a57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:12:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep weapon sounds playing on every shot

Regression: start() destroyed the player on any exception, and this Sound lives
in the Asset cache for the whole game, so the first failed restart silenced the
weapon permanently. Symbian/Nokia reject setMediaTime()/setLoopCount() while a
player is STARTED, which is exactly the state during rapid fire.

- stop a running player before seeking instead of throwing
- rebuild a closed/broken player lazily from the cached object (prepare/recover)
- remember an unusable file so it is not re-parsed on every shot
- destroy() no longer implies the sound can never play again
- drop the dead getLoopCount() accessor ProGuard stripped anyway
