+/**
+ * Sound wrapper that degrades to silence instead of failing.
+ *
+ * Handset realities handled here:
+ *  - MMAPI may be missing, or refuse the codec: every call returns quietly.
+ *  - A phone rejects setMediaTime()/setLoopCount() while the player is already
+ *    PLAYING (Symbian/Nokia do), and a weapon fires again long before the
+ *    previous shot finished. Retrying in the right state is what keeps the
+ *    second, third and hundredth shot audible.
+ *  - Loading is lazy and a missing file is a no-op, not a thrown exception.
+ *  - Recovering from a broken player must REBUILD it: this object lives in the
+ *    Asset cache for the whole game, so a destroyed player here means a
+ *    permanently silent weapon.
+ */
